B: I think we need Frank Worsley. He is an excellent navigator.
A: A good navigator is the most important thing for such a journey.
B: Yes. Without him, we could easily lose our way on the rough sea.
A: What about Tom Crean? He is strong, brave, and full of energy.
B: Perfect. We will need his strength to row for days without rest.
A: Then it is settled. Worsley to guide us, and Crean for his power.
B: Let''s tell the captain. The sooner we set off, the better.', '两人为救援船挑选另外两名水手:B 推荐沃斯利,因为他是出色的领航员;A 说领航员对这样的航行最重要;还选了汤姆·克林,因为他强壮勇敢、精力充沛,需要他的力气连日划船;两人决定告诉船长,越早出发越好。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What are the two speakers trying to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Choose sailors for the rescue boat.","Repair the broken ship.","Cook dinner for the crew.","Find a place to camp."]},{"q":"Why do they want Frank Worsley?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He is the youngest sailor.","He is an excellent navigator.","He is the best cook.","He owns the boat."]},{"q":"Why is a navigator so important for the journey?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["So they will not lose their way on the rough sea.","To catch more penguins.","To keep everyone warm.","To carry the heaviest bags."]},{"q":"Why do they choose Tom Crean?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Because he is quiet and shy.","Because they need his strength to row for days.","Because he can read maps.","Because he is good at advertising."]},{"q":"What do they decide to do next?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Wait for a week.","Look for more food.","Tell the captain and set off soon.","Go back to sleep."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U4');
In truth, courage is not the absence of fear.
It is the choice to act well even while you are afraid.
Real courage often shows itself in small, quiet actions.
Anyone can learn to be braver, one step at a time.', '许多人认为勇敢的英雄从不害怕;其实勇气并非没有恐惧,而是在害怕时仍选择做正确的事;真正的勇气常常体现在微小而安静的行动中;任何人都能一步一步学会更勇敢。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What do many people wrongly believe about heroes?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["That they are very rich.","That they live forever.","That they are always tall.","That they never feel afraid."]},{"q":"According to the passage, what is courage?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Acting well even while afraid.","Never trying anything.","Avoiding all danger.","Feeling no emotion."]},{"q":"Where does real courage often show itself?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only on television.","In small, quiet actions.","Only in famous battles.","Only among rich people."]},{"q":"What does the passage say about becoming braver?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It is impossible.","Only heroes can do it.","Anyone can learn it step by step.","It happens by luck."]},{"q":"What is the main message of the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Heroes are born, not made.","Fear should always stop us.","Only the strong are brave.","Courage means acting despite fear."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U4');
B: Of course it was. But I refused to let blindness end the life I loved.
A: How did you find your way up without being able to see?
B: I felt every hold with my hands and listened to my friends'' voices.
A: That must have taken years of practice and patience.
B: It did. I trained my body to trust touch and sound instead of sight.
A: What would you say to young people who face hard problems?
B: The biggest mountains we climb are often the ones inside our minds.', '记者采访一位失明后仍登山的攀登者:他承认害怕,但拒绝让失明终结自己热爱的生活;他靠双手感觉每个抓握点、靠朋友的声音找路;这需要多年练习,让身体学会信任触觉和听觉;他对面对困难的年轻人说:我们攀登的最大的山,往往在自己心里。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What difficulty did the climber face?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He had lost his sight.","He had broken his leg.","He had no money.","He could not swim."]},{"q":"How did he find his way up the mountain?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["By using a map.","By feeling holds and listening to friends.","By following painted signs.","By waiting for daylight."]},{"q":"What did the years of training teach his body to do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To run faster than others.","To need no rest at all.","To trust touch and sound instead of sight.","To climb only small hills."]},{"q":"What does he tell young people who face hard problems?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["To give up quickly.","To avoid all mountains.","To wait for help.","The biggest mountains are inside our minds."]},{"q":"How did the climber feel about the climb?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It was frightening, but he refused to give up.","It was easy and boring.","He felt no fear at all.","He regretted ever trying."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U4');
The secret is to break it into small, simple steps.
Do not ask how to finish everything at once.
Just ask what you can do in the next hour.
Many small steps, taken with hope, can carry you a very long way.', '当问题显得太大时,它会在我们开始之前就让我们停步;秘诀是把它拆成小而简单的步骤;别问如何一次完成全部,只问下一个小时你能做什么;许多带着希望迈出的小步,能把你带到很远的地方。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What can a problem that feels too big do to us?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Make us rich.","Stop us before we begin.","Solve itself quickly.","Make us sleep."]},{"q":"What is the secret the speaker gives?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To ignore the problem.","To ask others to do it.","To break it into small steps.","To wait for next year."]},{"q":"What should we NOT ask, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["What to eat tonight.","Where to sleep.","Who our friends are.","How to finish everything at once."]},{"q":"What should we ask instead?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["What we can do in the next hour.","Why life is unfair.","When the holiday starts.","Who is to blame."]},{"q":"What can many small steps do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Waste all your time.","Carry you a very long way.","Make problems bigger.","Stop you from trying."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U4');
B: Yes, I''ve been training every single day to build up my endurance.
A: Good. The cold and the long marches will test all of us.
B: I know. I''ve also been reading about how others survived such journeys.
A: That''s wise. Their stories can teach us how to handle real danger.
B: What worries me most is the rough sea on the way there.
A: Stay calm and trust the team. Together we can face anything.
B: You''re right. With good preparation and courage, we''ll be fine.', '两人谈下个月出发的远征:B 说每天训练以增强耐力;A 说严寒和长途行军会考验大家;B 还读了别人如何在这种旅程中生存;A 说这些故事能教人应对真正的危险;B 最担心途中汹涌的海;A 让他保持冷静、信任团队;B 同意,有充分准备和勇气就没问题。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When does the expedition leave?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Tomorrow.","Next year.","Next month.","This evening."]},{"q":"How has B been preparing?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["By sleeping all day.","By buying new furniture.","By doing nothing.","By training every day to build endurance."]},{"q":"Why has B been reading about other journeys?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To learn how others survived such trips.","To pass the time only.","Because there is nothing else to do.","To find a new ship."]},{"q":"What worries B the most?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The price of food.","The rough sea on the way there.","The lack of friends.","The boring training."]},{"q":"What advice does A give B?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Travel alone.","Cancel the trip.","Stay calm and trust the team.","Forget all preparation."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U4');
Almost everyone meets adversity at some point in life.
Do not be afraid to ask a friend or teacher for help.
A worry that is shared with someone always feels lighter.
This difficult time is only one chapter in your long story.', '如果你正经历艰难时光,请记住你并不孤单;几乎每个人在人生某个阶段都会遭遇逆境;不要害怕向朋友或老师求助;与人分担的忧虑总会轻一些;这段艰难只是你漫长故事中的一个篇章。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the speaker want listeners in hard times to remember?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["That they should hide their feelings.","That nothing will ever change.","That they are weak.","That they are not alone."]},{"q":"According to the passage, who meets adversity?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Almost everyone at some point.","Only a few unlucky people.","Only the poor.","Only explorers."]},{"q":"What does the speaker say about asking for help?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Never do it.","Do not be afraid to ask a friend or teacher.","Only ask family.","Help is useless."]},{"q":"Why is a shared worry better?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It costs money.","It makes friends angry.","It always feels lighter.","It wastes time."]},{"q":"How does the speaker describe this difficult time?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["As the end of everything.","As a permanent state.","As something to be ashamed of.","As only one chapter in a long story."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U4');

-- ===== 6) 写作 1篇 =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_writing_prompts WHERE volume='elective3' AND unit='U4';

I was sorry to hear that you failed the exam and feel like giving up. Please don''t lose heart—one setback does not decide your whole future.

Think of Ernest Shackleton. When his ship was crushed by ice, he and his crew were trapped for months in the freezing Antarctic. Yet they never gave up. By taking one small step at a time and supporting one another, every single man came home alive.

You can do the same. Study a little each day, and talk to someone you trust when you feel low. This hard time is only one chapter in your story.

I''m sure you''ll get through it. Stay strong!

Yours,
Li Hua', '【15 分制】A 档(13-15):五要素齐全、组织有条理、语言准确多样;B 档(10-12):要点较全、少量错误;C 档(7-9):要点偏少、句型简单;D 档(0-6):内容不完整、错误多。', '["Please don''t lose heart—one setback does not decide your whole future.","When his ship was crushed by ice, Shackleton and his crew never gave up.","By taking one small step at a time and supporting one another, every single man came home alive.","This hard time is only one chapter in your story."]'::jsonb, '[{"wrong":"I am sorry to hear that you failed in the exam.","correct":"I am sorry to hear that you failed the exam.","note":"fail the exam 直接跟宾语,不加 in。"},{"wrong":"They have been never give up.","correct":"They never gave up.","note":"讲过去完成的事用一般过去时;''never give up'' 动词须用过去式 gave。"},{"wrong":"I am sure you will get through with it.","correct":"I am sure you will get through it.","note":"get through sth = 度过/熬过,直接跟宾语,不加 with。"}]'::jsonb, '【鼓励信结构】
称呼:Dear Tom,
第1段 安慰:I was sorry to hear … Please don''t lose heart.
第2段 故事:Think of Shackleton, who … never gave up … came home alive.
第3段 建议+信心:Study a little each day … I''m sure you''ll get through it.
落款:Yours, Li Hua', 2, 'elective3', 'U4');

